    "title": "Here's who made the 2025-2026 season roster cut for the Fort Valley State Wildcats - Warner Robins Today",
    "text": "Fort Valley State Wildcats release roster of 17 players to open the season.\nThey look to set the tone as they open the year away against the Tuskegee Golden Tigers on Nov. 20 at James Center Arena.\nThe Wildcats want to improve upon their record of 7-18 last season.\nHere is their full 2025-2026 roster\n20 — A’rieonna Booker — Guard — 5′11″ — Hometown: Augusta\n1 — Aaniyah Allen — Guard — 5′5″ — Hometown: Elberton\n34 — Akirya Robinson — Guard — 5′9″ — Hometown: Columbus\n24 — Delissa Kier — Center — 6′5″ — Hometown: Valdosta\n3 — Grace East — Guard — 5′7″ — Hometown: Gastonia\n50 — Haneefat Adanijo — Guard — 5′10″ — Hometown: Dacula\n31 — India McIntosh — Center — 6′3″ — Hometown: Jonesboro\n45 — Jalexicia Hargrove — Center — 6′0″ — Hometown: Sparta\n4 — Jatiana Chambers — Guard — 5′3″ — Hometown: Albany\n21 — Jewel Harwell — Forward — 5′10″ — Hometown: Riverview\n13 — Julia Baker — Guard — 5′9″ — Hometown: McDonough\n12 — Kimora Wade — Forward — 6′0″ — Hometown: Valdosta\n10 — Madisyn Ogburn — Guard — 5′5″ — Hometown: Clarksville\n44 — Makayla Arnold — Center — 6′2″ — Hometown: Atlanta\n22 — Marley Bell — Forward — 5′10″ — Hometown: Montgomery\n11 — Reya Johnson — Guard — 5′7″ — Hometown: Statesboro\n5 — Tiana Gongora — Guard — 5′10″ — Hometown: Charlotte",
